1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,877
Eli looked up from his phone just as the

2
00:00:03,877 --> 00:00:07,754
train doors closed. His station slid past the window.

3
00:00:07,754 --> 00:00:11,631
He had been holding the ticket for twenty minutes.

4
00:00:12,051 --> 00:00:16,505
Nothing urgent had happened on the screen. Someone had

5
00:00:16,505 --> 00:00:20,959
rearranged a bedroom. Someone had explained a controversy. A

6
00:00:20,959 --> 00:00:25,413
stranger had bought a car he would never drive.

7
00:00:25,833 --> 00:00:29,179
Each item lasted a moment. Together, they had carried

8
00:00:29,179 --> 00:00:32,526
him across the city. He locked the phone and

9
00:00:32,526 --> 00:00:35,872
saw his own tired face in the dark glass.

10
00:00:36,292 --> 00:00:39,403
By the time he walked home, his dinner was

11
00:00:39,403 --> 00:00:42,514
cold. A message from his friend Leon waited beside

12
00:00:42,514 --> 00:00:45,626
a delivery advertisement. Still on for Saturday? He answered

13
00:00:45,626 --> 00:00:48,737
yes.

14
00:00:49,157 --> 00:00:52,970
They had planned to cook together, something they used

15
00:00:52,970 --> 00:00:56,784
to do when their apartments were smaller and their

16
00:00:56,784 --> 00:01:00,598
evenings felt longer. Eli added it to his calendar.

17
00:01:01,018 --> 00:01:05,092
Then he lay down for a minute. The phone

18
00:01:05,092 --> 00:01:09,166
rested above his face. One clip ended exactly where

19
00:01:09,166 --> 00:01:13,239
the next began, leaving no natural place to stop.

20
00:01:13,659 --> 00:01:17,849
Saturday arrived. He bought tomatoes, bread, and a lemon.

21
00:01:17,849 --> 00:01:22,039
He imagined music in the kitchen, an unhurried meal,

22
00:01:22,039 --> 00:01:26,229
and a conversation that did not happen through messages.

23
00:01:26,649 --> 00:01:30,709
While the kettle boiled, he opened the feed. A

24
00:01:30,709 --> 00:01:34,768
notification led to a comment. The comment led somewhere

25
00:01:34,768 --> 00:01:38,827
else. The kettle clicked off behind his shoulder.

26
00:01:39,247 --> 00:01:42,946
Leon knocked twice before Eli heard him. They laughed

27
00:01:42,946 --> 00:01:46,644
about it. Eli placed the phone beside the chopping

28
00:01:46,644 --> 00:01:50,342
board, face up, close enough to check between slices.

29
00:01:50,762 --> 00:01:54,230
Leon started telling him about a job interview. Halfway

30
00:01:54,230 --> 00:01:57,698
through, the screen lit up. Eli glanced down, nodded

31
00:01:57,698 --> 00:02:01,165
at the wrong moment, and asked a question Leon

32
00:02:01,165 --> 00:02:04,633
had already answered.

33
00:02:05,053 --> 00:02:08,582
There was a small silence. Not a fight. Leon

34
00:02:08,582 --> 00:02:12,111
looked at the tomatoes and said, I can tell

35
00:02:12,111 --> 00:02:15,640
you later. Eli had heard that sentence before.

36
00:02:16,060 --> 00:02:19,325
He wanted to explain that he was listening. But

37
00:02:19,325 --> 00:02:22,590
he could not repeat what his friend had just

38
00:02:22,590 --> 00:02:25,855
said. The defense dissolved before it reached his mouth.

39
00:02:26,275 --> 00:02:31,717
On the screen, another item was always waiting. A

40
00:02:31,717 --> 00:02:37,158
cue invited a check. Checking revealed something new. Sometimes

41
00:02:37,158 --> 00:02:42,600
useful, sometimes empty. Either way, there was another cue.

42
00:02:43,020 --> 00:02:45,553
The service did not know that this was his

43
00:02:45,553 --> 00:02:48,086
one free afternoon with Leon. It could count another

44
00:02:48,086 --> 00:02:50,619
interaction. It could not count the conversation he had

45
00:02:50,619 --> 00:02:53,152
missed.

46
00:02:53,572 --> 00:02:56,471
An advertisement filled the display. He had not paid

47
00:02:56,471 --> 00:02:59,369
for the feed. Yet his afternoon had helped make

48
00:02:59,369 --> 00:03:02,268
its audience valuable to someone buying a place inside

49
00:03:02,268 --> 00:03:05,167
it.

50
00:03:05,587 --> 00:03:08,622
Eli turned the phone over. Then it vibrated against

51
00:03:08,622 --> 00:03:11,658
the wooden counter. His hand moved before he decided

52
00:03:11,658 --> 00:03:14,694
to move it. He stopped with his fingers touching

53
00:03:14,694 --> 00:03:17,730
the case.

54
00:03:18,150 --> 00:03:20,833
He carried it into the hallway and put it

55
00:03:20,833 --> 00:03:23,517
in a drawer. There was nothing impressive about the

56
00:03:23,517 --> 00:03:26,201
gesture. He simply wanted the next choice to require

57
00:03:26,201 --> 00:03:28,885
standing up.

58
00:03:29,305 --> 00:03:32,262
Back in the kitchen, he asked Leon to start

59
00:03:32,262 --> 00:03:35,219
again. Not because the interruption had never happened, but

60
00:03:35,219 --> 00:03:38,175
because it had. This time he put down the

61
00:03:38,175 --> 00:03:41,132
knife.

62
00:03:41,552 --> 00:03:45,145
The interview had gone badly. Leon was embarrassed. Eli

63
00:03:45,145 --> 00:03:48,738
listened without collecting an answer in advance. There was

64
00:03:48,738 --> 00:03:52,331
no clever lesson, just a friend who needed a

65
00:03:52,331 --> 00:03:55,924
few minutes.

66
00:03:56,344 --> 00:03:59,516
They burned the first piece of bread. The smoke

67
00:03:59,516 --> 00:04:02,688
alarm complained. Leon laughed, then Eli laughed too. It

68
00:04:02,688 --> 00:04:05,860
was the first thing that afternoon he knew he

69
00:04:05,860 --> 00:04:09,033
would remember.

70
00:04:09,453 --> 00:04:13,907
After dinner, he opened the drawer. Several notifications had

71
00:04:13,907 --> 00:04:18,362
accumulated. Most could have waited. One message mattered. He

72
00:04:18,362 --> 00:04:22,817
answered it and left the rest for later.

73
00:04:23,237 --> 00:04:26,747
That night, he checked which alerts he actually wanted.

74
00:04:26,747 --> 00:04:30,256
Messages from people stayed. Promotional reminders went. He was

75
00:04:30,256 --> 00:04:33,766
not deleting modern life. He was making its entrances

76
00:04:33,766 --> 00:04:37,275
less noisy.

77
00:04:37,695 --> 00:04:40,927
He drew a simple boundary for ordinary evenings: choose

78
00:04:40,927 --> 00:04:44,159
a reason, use the tool, leave when the reason

79
00:04:44,159 --> 00:04:47,391
is finished. A boundary, not a promise never to

80
00:04:47,391 --> 00:04:50,622
get distracted.

81
00:04:51,042 --> 00:04:53,857
The next morning, he reached for the empty bedside

82
00:04:53,857 --> 00:04:56,671
table. His phone was charging across the room. For

83
00:04:56,671 --> 00:04:59,486
a moment, he did not know what to do

84
00:04:59,486 --> 00:05:02,300
with his hand.

85
00:05:02,720 --> 00:05:05,776
He opened the curtain. Rain had stopped during the

86
00:05:05,776 --> 00:05:08,832
night. Water trembled along the railing. He had lived

87
00:05:08,832 --> 00:05:11,889
beside that view for years without noticing how the

88
00:05:11,889 --> 00:05:14,945
drops gathered.

89
00:05:15,365 --> 00:05:18,493
On Monday, he took the same train. He checked

90
00:05:18,493 --> 00:05:21,622
the route, answered a message, and put the phone

91
00:05:21,622 --> 00:05:24,751
away before the carriage reached the tunnel.

92
00:05:25,171 --> 00:05:28,498
At lunch, he slipped back into scrolling and stayed

93
00:05:28,498 --> 00:05:31,826
longer than he meant to. He noticed the time,

94
00:05:31,826 --> 00:05:35,153
felt annoyed, and resisted turning one lapse into a

95
00:05:35,153 --> 00:05:38,481
verdict about himself.

96
00:05:38,901 --> 00:05:42,967
He wrote down where it happened: tired, hungry, waiting

97
00:05:42,967 --> 00:05:47,033
alone. That told him more than calling himself weak.

98
00:05:47,033 --> 00:05:51,099
Next time, he could eat before opening the feed.

99
00:05:51,519 --> 00:05:54,555
He still enjoyed things he found online. Some made

100
00:05:54,555 --> 00:05:57,591
him laugh. Some taught him something. The difference was

101
00:05:57,591 --> 00:06:00,627
whether he had chosen the visit or merely followed

102
00:06:00,627 --> 00:06:03,662
the nearest light.

103
00:06:04,082 --> 00:06:07,199
A week later, Leon sent a photograph of another

104
00:06:07,199 --> 00:06:10,316
questionable loaf. Eli smiled, called him, and made plans.

105
00:06:10,316 --> 00:06:13,433
The phone was useful. That had never been the

106
00:06:13,433 --> 00:06:16,550
enemy.

107
00:06:16,970 --> 00:06:20,072
His attention was not limitless. Spending it in one

108
00:06:20,072 --> 00:06:23,174
place meant being absent from another. He could not

109
00:06:23,174 --> 00:06:26,276
recover every lost hour, but he could decide where

110
00:06:26,276 --> 00:06:29,378
this one went.

111
00:06:29,798 --> 00:06:32,937
That evening, he stepped outside without reaching for the

112
00:06:32,937 --> 00:06:36,077
drawer. The city had no automatic next item. He

113
00:06:36,077 --> 00:06:39,216
had to choose a direction, and then look where

114
00:06:39,216 --> 00:06:42,356
he was going.

115
00:06:42,776 --> 00:06:45,462
Someone will always have another reason for you to

116
00:06:45,462 --> 00:06:48,148
stay. Before you give them the rest of your

117
00:06:48,148 --> 00:06:50,834
evening, ask who or what you meant to be

118
00:06:50,834 --> 00:06:53,520
present for.
